 <div class="hero"><span class="hero-badge">Game purchase guide</span><h1 id="article-title">Arknights Monthly Card and 300-roll Limited Headhunting planning</h1>
 <!-- reading-tools:start --><div class="reading-tools" data-reading-tools><button type="button" disabled aria-pressed="false">Read later</button><a href="/en/articles/#reading-library">Saved articles & reading history</a><span role="status"></span></div><!-- reading-tools:end -->
 
-<p class="article-region-scope">Language: English · US reference. Offers depend on your Google Play country and account.</p><p class="hero-meta">Published <time data-article-date="published" datetime="2026-09-13">September 13, 2026</time> · Updated <time data-article-date="modified" datetime="2026-09-13">September 13, 2026</time> · Official info checked <time data-article-date="official-verified" datetime="2026-09-13">September 13, 2026</time> · Official sources checked: September 13, 2026</p></div>
+<p class="article-region-scope">Language: English · US reference. Offers depend on your Google Play country and account.</p><p class="hero-meta">Published <time data-article-date="published" datetime="2026-09-13">September 13, 2026</time> · Updated <time data-article-date="modified" datetime="2026-09-13">September 13, 2026</time> · Official info checked <time data-article-date="official-verified" datetime="2026-09-13">September 13, 2026</time></p></div>
 <article class="content">
 <div class="intro">An April 2026 Global notice says the featured limited Operator is awarded after 300 rolls once, while the Data Contract Shop also shows some older limited Operators at 200 contracts. The banner notice, not a static old table, is the source of truth.</div>
 <div class="decision-box"><strong>Which route makes sense?</strong><p>Separate a current 300-roll featured guarantee from Data Contract exchange targets.</p></div>
-<nav class="intl-article-toc" aria-label="Table of contents"><h2 id="article-section-1">Contents</h2><ol><li><a href="#official-source-scope">What the official sources say</a></li><li><a href="#google-play-rule">Google Play Points: what counts</a></li><li><a href="#decision-guide">Which route makes sense?</a></li><li><a href="#before-paying">Before you pay</a></li></ol></nav>
+<nav class="intl-article-toc" aria-label="Contents"><h2 id="article-section-1">Contents</h2><ol><li><a href="#official-source-scope">What the official sources say</a></li><li><a href="#decision-guide">Which route makes sense?</a></li><li><a href="#before-paying">Before you pay</a></li></ol></nav>
 <section class="section" id="official-source-scope"><h2 id="article-section-2">What the official sources say</h2><p>An April 2026 Global notice says the featured limited Operator is awarded after 300 rolls once, while the Data Contract Shop also shows some older limited Operators at 200 contracts. The banner notice, not a static old table, is the source of truth.</p><p>Official terminology used on this page:</p><ul><li><strong>Arknights</strong></li><li><strong>Monthly Card</strong></li><li><strong>Limited Headhunting</strong></li><li><strong>Headhunting Data Contract</strong></li></ul></section>
-<section class="section" id="google-play-rule"><h2 id="article-section-3">Google Play Points: what counts</h2><p>In the United States, Bronze earns 1 point per US$1 on eligible Google Play purchases. Higher levels raise the base rate; tax is excluded and the highest eligible promotional earn rate applies.</p><p>Google Play Points are earned only when the purchase is processed as an eligible Google Play transaction. A publisher Web Store, PC client, console store or other external checkout may have its own discount or rewards, but that does not automatically make it eligible for Google Play Points.</p></section>
-<section class="section" id="decision-guide"><h2 id="article-section-4">Which route makes sense?</h2><ul><li>Separate a current 300-roll featured guarantee from Data Contract exchange targets.</li><li>Treat Monthly Card value as gradual resources, not instant 300-roll funding.</li><li>Play Points come from paid Google Play transactions, not spending Orundum.</li></ul></section>
-<section class="section" id="before-paying"><h2 id="article-section-5">Before you pay</h2><p>Check the exact banner series, dates and 200/300-contract target.</p><p>Recheck the live price, supported country, account and checkout provider immediately before payment.</p></section>
-<div class="cta-box"><h3 id="article-section-6">Check the purchase in the game calculator</h3><p>Use the amount and final earn rate shown on the Google Play account that will actually pay.</p><a class="cta-btn" href="/en/games/arknights/">Open game calculator</a></div>
-<aside class="official-source-note"><h2 id="article-section-7">Official sources checked</h2><ul><li><a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/9077192?co=GENIE.CountryCode%3DUS&amp;hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play Points earning rules — United States</a></li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/answer/9080348?co=GENIE.CountryCode%3DUS&amp;hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play Points levels — United States</a></li><li><a href="https://www.arknights.global/news/2926" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Arknights Global 2026 Limited Headhunting notice</a></li></ul></aside>
-<section class="section"><h2 id="article-section-8">FAQ</h2><h3 id="article-section-9">Is every limited Operator always 300 contracts?</h3><p>No. Current official notices show some older limited Operators at 200.</p></section>
